<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- macOS will not even consider a location request from a process that has
       not said why it wants one; without this key the request is denied before
       any prompt appears, which is indistinguishable from a broken button.

       The key is here so that a window able to ask CAN ask. It is not what
       makes "Here & now" work: that is answered from the device's own clock
       and the bundled city list, with no permission of any kind. This only
       buys the sharper answer when the system is willing to give it. -->
  <key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Nirayana uses your location only to set the place for a chart cast for here and now. It stays on this Mac and is never sent anywhere.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
